From: Oever Gonzalez <software@notengobattery.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7996: make the chip full-reset path NPU-aware

mt7996_mac_full_reset() resets WFDMA and the whole wireless subsystem,
then re-downloads firmware -- and never says a word to the NPU. The NPU
keeps DMA-ing into rings that no longer exist, the writes come back as
PCIe completion timeouts, and every one of those raises another MCU
command timeout, which queues another full reset. The result is the
recovery loop reporting "chip full reset failed" every few seconds until
the board is power-cycled.

This is not a debug knob nobody reaches. dev->recovery.restart is set
from mt7996_mcu_parse_response() on any MCU command timeout and from
mt7996_reset() on a WM/WA firmware watchdog, so on an offload-enabled
board the automatic recovery path is the one that bricks the chip.

Reloading the module does recover it, and the difference is one call:
probe issues airoha_npu_wlan_init_reserved_memory(), which hands the
NPU the tx-bufid, pkt, tx-pkt and BA region bases and makes its firmware
rebuild the buffer pools behind them. Nothing else in the driver ever
issues it, so the pools survive every in-place reset unchanged.

Do that, and re-bind the ring addresses, once the firmware is back up.
Both belong after mt7996_mcu_init_firmware(): the pool rebuild ends by
clearing the NPU's force-to-CPU flag, so running it earlier lets the NPU
resume into a chip that has just been reset and has nothing loaded --
which reproduces the very completion-timeout storm this is meant to fix.

Neither failure is fatal to the restart -- the interrupts stay masked
from the reset, so a failed rebind leaves offload down rather than
pointed at freed rings -- but both are worth a line in the log.

Also mask the NPU interrupts before the wfsys reset rather than after
it, which is the order the unload path already uses.

--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -513,6 +513,18 @@
 				      &dev->mt76.q_rx[MT_RXQ_NPU1]);
 }
 
+int __mt7996_npu_mem_reinit(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
+{
+	struct airoha_npu *npu;
+
+	npu = rcu_dereference_protected(dev->mt76.mmio.npu, &dev->mt76.mutex);
+	if (!npu)
+		return 0;
+
+	/* the only call that makes NPU firmware rebuild its buffer pools */
+	return airoha_npu_wlan_init_reserved_memory(npu);
+}
+
 int __mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
 	struct airoha_npu *npu;
--- a/mt7996/mt7996.h
+++ b/mt7996/mt7996.h
@@ -1005,6 +1005,7 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_MT7996_NPU
 int __mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev);
+int __mt7996_npu_mem_reinit(struct mt7996_dev *dev);
 int mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev);
 int mt7996_npu_hw_stop(struct mt7996_dev *dev);
 int mt7996_npu_rx_queues_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev);
@@ -1013,6 +1014,11 @@
 {
 	return 0;
 }
+
+static inline int __mt7996_npu_mem_reinit(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
 
 static inline int mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -995,6 +995,9 @@
 	    !mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed))
 		mt7996_rro_msdu_page_map_free(dev);
 
+	/* the NPU interrupts across the reset window otherwise */
+	mt76_npu_disable_irqs(&dev->mt76);
+
 	/* reset wfsys */
 	if (force)
 		mt7996_wfsys_reset(dev);
@@ -1005,7 +1008,6 @@
 	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed))
 		mtk_wed_device_dma_reset(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed);
 
-	mt76_npu_disable_irqs(&dev->mt76);
 	mt7996_dma_disable(dev, force);
 	mt76_wed_dma_reset(&dev->mt76);
 
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2292,7 +2292,7 @@
 {
 	struct mt76_dev *mdev = &dev->mt76;
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy;
-	int i, ret;
+	int i, ret, err;
 
 	if (dev->hif2) {
 		mt76_wr(dev, MT_INT1_MASK_CSR, 0x0);
@@ -2364,6 +2364,18 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* rebuild the pools only once the chip can answer again: probe does
+	 * this against a live wireless side and nothing else ever issues it
+	 */
+	err = __mt7996_npu_mem_reinit(dev);
+	if (err)
+		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "npu memory re-init failed: %d\n", err);
+
+	/* the NPU still points at rings this reset invalidated */
+	err = __mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
+	if (err)
+		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "npu offload rebind failed: %d\n", err);
+
 	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) &&
 	    mt7996_has_hwrro(dev)) {
 		u32 wed_irq_mask = dev->mt76.mmio.irqmask |
